{"step_index":70,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T08:32:47Z","content":"## BE‑1 (Sensory‑Motor Engine – “Hands”) – Concrete Task List  \n\nThe **BE‑1** sub‑system is responsible for **capturing the screen, detecting the hand / gaze, mapping that to a UI element, and performing OS‑level input**.  \nBelow are the exact items from the previous roadmap that belong **solely to BE‑1** (everything else – policy, memory, HUD, canvas – is handled by other teams).\n\n| # | Task | Description | Deliverable / Artefact |\n|---|------|-------------|------------------------|\n| **1** | **Create shared protobuf contracts** (actuator + event) | `actuator.proto` (gRPC service) and `event.proto` (ZeroMQ messages) must be placed in `common/proto/` so all teams can import them. | `actuator.proto`, `event.proto` (generated `_pb2.py` files). |\n| **2** | **Generate SQLite DB schema** (optional for BE‑1 – only to log its own events) | Create `system_state.db` with `episode` table; BE‑1 will write its own `Result` rows. | `system_state.db` with `episode` table. |\n| **3** | **Screen Capture Module** (`app/screen_perception`) | Use **dxcam** (or fallback to **mss**) to grab frames; use **pywinauto** to enumerate top‑level windows → build `ScreenEvent` protobuf. | `app/screen_perception/capture.py` (publishes `screen.events`). |\n| **4** | **Vision / Hand Detection Stub** (`app/vision`) | Initial placeholder returning a static point; later replaced by MediaPipe. | `app/vision/hand.py` (function `get_hand_point`). |\n| **5** | **Calibration Utility** (`app/calibration`) | Compute homography matrix from a 3‑point grid (store matrix for later use). | `app/calibration/calib.py` (function `compute_homography`). |\n| **6** | **Mapper** (`app/mapper`) | Convert a screen‑space point (after homography) → UI element ID using the UI graph from step 3. | `app/mapper/map.py` (`map_point_to_element`). |\n| **7** | **ZeroMQ Bus Helper** (`app/bus`) | Simple wrapper to publish `screen.events`, `hands.intent`, `hands.result`; also to subscribe when needed. | `app/bus/bus.py`. |\n| **8** | **OS Actuator (Input Injection)** (`app/os_actuator`) | Use **pynput** (mouse/keyboard) + **pywin32** (window focus) to implement `move`, `click`, `drag`, `type_keys`, `focus_window`. This will be called by the gRPC server. | `app/os_actuator/actuator.py` (functions performing real OS actions). |\n| **9** | **gRPC Actuator Server** (`app/grpc_server`) | Implements the `Actuator` service defined in `actuator.proto`. Validates HMAC token, calls the functions from **Task 8**. | `app/grpc_server/server.py`. |\n| **10** | **Coordinator / Pipeline Runner** (`run_pipeline.py`) | Glue code that starts the screen publisher, subscribes to `screen.events`, obtains a hand point, maps it, and publishes `hands.intent`. Also writes `hands.result` after actuation (future step). | `run_pipeline.py`. |\n| **11** | **Testing & Verification** | • Unit tests for each module (`pytest`). <br>• Integration test that runs the publisher + intent worker + gRPC stub together. | `tests/` folder with test files. |\n| **12** | **Documentation** | README section that explains: how to start the screen publisher, how to run the gRPC server, how to invoke the pipeline, and how to check logs/SQLite. | `README.md` (BE‑1 specific section). |\n\n---\n\n### Immediate “Next‑Step” Priorities (first 4‑5 items)\n\n1. **Protobufs** – make sure `actuator.proto` and `event.proto` are in `common/proto/` and the Python stubs are generated (`grpc_tools.protoc`).  \n2. **Screen Capture** – get `app/screen_perception/capture.py` running and verify the ZeroMQ `screen.events` stream.  \n3. **Vision Stub** – implement the simple `get_hand_point` that returns a constant centre point.  \n4. **Mapper** – write `map_point_to_element` and test it against the UI list emitted by the screen capture.  \n5. **Publish `hands.intent`** – extend the pipeline (run\\_pipeline.py) so that after mapping you send an `Intent` on the bus.\n\nOnce these work end‑to‑end (hand point → intent), you can move on to the **real MediaPipe hand detection (Task 4 → replace stub)**, then **OS actuation + gRPC (Tasks 8‑9)**, and finally **logging to SQLite (Task 2)**.\n\n---\n\n### What *not* to implement as BE‑1 (for reference)\n\n| Item | Belongs to |\n|------|-------------|\n| Policy enforcement, HMAC token generation, violation publishing | **BE‑3** (Boundary Hypervisor) |\n| Episodic‑memory ingestion, drift detection, self‑healing control messages | **BE‑2** (Episodic Memory) |\n| HUD visualisation, overlay of screen + hand pointer | **FE‑1** (Mission Control & HUD) |\n| Canvas simulator, virtual cursor publishing | **FE‑2** (Spatial Canvas & Simulator) |\n| Global configuration files (`policy.json`) | **BE‑3** (or shared config repo) |\n\n---\n\n### Summary – What you should have now\n\n- **Virtual env** activated, all libraries installed.  \n- **Protobufs** compiled.  \n- **Screen capture** publishing a `ScreenEvent` every second.  \n- **Hand‑point stub** returning a centre coordinate.  \n- **Mapper** able to locate a UI element from that point.  \n- **ZeroMQ bus** ready (publish/subscribe helpers).  \n- **Skeleton gRPC server** listening (still a stub).  \n\nWhen you have those pieces running and can see the `hands.intent` messages on the bus, you’re ready to flesh out the real vision pipeline and the actuation layer.  \n\nLet me know which of the above items you’d like a concrete code template for, or if you want to run a quick test of the current pipeline. Happy coding! 🚀"}
